    "body": "This might not be so bad. We can just use [incrementally read](https://fetch.spec.whatwg.org/#body-incrementally-read).\r\n\r\nA few questions:\r\n\r\n- @noamr do you remember why we delay \"process link headers\" until after the first task is done feeding the HTML parser? It seems cleaner to do it before. I didn't find any clues in https://github.com/whatwg/html/pull/7622 .\r\n\r\n- What happens if we hit processBodyError? This means there was an error reading from the network socket or something. Based on my experiences as a user, I think browsers treat this as an end-of-stream, i.e. processBodyError = processEndOfBody?",
